WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.820
Game of Thrones prequel series, House of the
Dragon, is coming in 2022.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.490
It’s based on George RR Martin’s book
Fire And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.119
yet unfinished Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:27.579
Fire &amp; Blood covers the tales from the legendary
Aegon the Conqueror all the way up to the

00:00:27.579 --> 00:00:32.739
civil war, the Dance of the Dragons, that
nearly tore their dynasty apart, while Fire

00:00:32.739 --> 00:00:37.880
And Blood volume 2 will continue from where
part 1 ended, and will cover Blackyre rebellions

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:42.960
and go all the way to the Mad King and Robert's
Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.740
House of the Dragon is based on the Targaryen
history and therefore it's not surprising

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:51.120
that this show will feature many Targaryen
dragons, and the most powerful of them all

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.789
- Balerion the Black Dread.

00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:56.879
Balerion, called the Black Dread, was a dragon
of House Targaryen.

00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:02.829
He was ridden by King Aegon I Targaryen during
his Conquest, alongside his sister Queen Visenya's

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:06.460
Vhagar,
and his sister Queen Rhaenys's Meraxes.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:12.060
Other known riders of Balerion were King Maegor
I Targaryen, Princess Aerea Targaryen and

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.780
King Viserys I Targaryen.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:20.540
Balerion died of old age in 94 AC during the
reign of King Jaehaerys I Targaryen, being

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.069
around two hundred years old.

00:01:23.069 --> 00:01:25.180
Balerion's scales and wings were black.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.150
His fire was black, sometimes with swirls
of red.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:33.020
When he was in the fullness of his power,
his flames could melt steel and stone, and

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.460
fuse sand into glass.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.849
Balerion was named after the ancient god of
the Valyrian Freehold.

00:01:38.849 --> 00:01:43.429
He was born in Valyria, and was one of the
five dragons Aenar Targaryen brought with

00:01:43.429 --> 00:01:47.729
him when he fled to Dragonstone to survive
the Doom of Valyria.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:52.349
After the other four of Aenar's dragons died,
Balerion became the last creature to have

00:01:52.349 --> 00:01:55.400
seen the Valyrian Freehold in its prime.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:59.369
Balerion was the largest of all the Targaryen
dragons since Aegon's Conquest.

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:05.349
His wingspan was so large that his shadow
could engulf entire towns when he passed overhead.

00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:09.820
His teeth were as long as swords, and his
jaws were large enough to swallow an aurochs

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.670
whole, or even one of the hairy mammoths that
are said to roam the cold wastes beyond the

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.030
Port of Ibben.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:20.140
By 93 AC, Balerion had finally stopped growing.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:24.120
He had grown sluggish and heavy and was difficult
to rouse.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.280
When Prince Viserys Targaryen claimed the
dragon that year, the dragon struggled to

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.459
take to the air.

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:32.189
But back to prime Balerion.

00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:37.129
Balerion was claimed by Lord Aegon Targaryen,
sometime before he married his sisters Visenya

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:38.730
and Rhaenys.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:44.090
Aegon became involved in the wars in the Disputed
Lands when Pentos and Tyrosh approached him,

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:49.950
inviting him to join a grand alliance against
Volantis, and he chose to heed their call.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.710
Mounting Balerion, he flew east to meet the
Prince of Pentos and the magisters of the

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:58.879
Free City,
then flew to Lys in time to set ablaze a Volantene

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:01.110
fleet trying to take the city.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.620
Afterwards, Aegon turned his attention to
conquering the Seven Kingdoms, during which

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.709
he flew on Balerion.

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:12.780
Aegon then began planning the invasion of
Westeros long before launching the attack,

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:18.519
spending time incognito on Balerion in air,
scouting Westeros, visiting Westerosi cities

00:03:18.519 --> 00:03:24.030
and castles and gaining intelligence on the
different houses, their lords and their vassals.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:28.830
Aegon, his two sister-wives and their three
dragons led a scant few thousand troops in

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.019
invading the entire continent of Westeros.

00:03:32.019 --> 00:03:36.590
Aegon descended on Lords Mooton and Darklyn,
killing both of them during Aegon's first

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.590
test.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:43.090
Next, Aegon took Balerion to Harrenhal, where
King Harren Hoare took refuge in his formidable

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.090
fortress.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:49.030
When Hoare had not yielded by sunset, he took
Balerion high up and descended inside the

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.739
castle walls, and put the castle to flame.

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:58.510
Balerion's dragonfire burned so hot that the
towers of Harrenhal went up like candles,

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:01.989
melting and twisting into the shapes they
retain to this day.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:06.730
King Harren and his sons all perished, ending
the line of House Hoare.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:11.780
Despite being vastly outnumbered, Aegon was
able to secure victory after victory using

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:12.780
Balerion.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:17.860
Aegon next rode Balerion in the Field of Fire,
beside his sisters on Vhagar and Meraxes.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:22.470
Vhagar was a she-dragon of House Targaryen
and like Balerion, she was also named for

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.639
one of the gods of Old Valyria.

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:28.750
Vhagar was large enough that one could ride
a horse down her gullet,

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.920
but not as large as Balerion nor as strong.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:36.080
It's also said that Vhagar's breath was so
hot that it could melt a knight's armor and

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:41.110
cook him inside, but not as hot as Balerion's
which could melt steel and stone.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:46.410
Meraxes, like Vhagar was also a she-dragon
of House Targaryen and like two of her siblings,

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:49.830
she was also named for one of the gods of
Old Valyria.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:54.090
Meraxes was larger than Vhagar, but smaller
than Balerion.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.780
Meraxes could swallow horses whole.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:01.530
Between the three dragons, four thousand men
were burned to death, including King Mern

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.490
IX Gardener, resulting in Targaryen victory.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:10.490
Aegon's army was defeated, but the Targaryen
dragons (Balerion, Meraxes, and Vhagar) allowed

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:15.590
Aegon to achieve a great victory at the Field
of Fire, which resulted in the death of Mern

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:19.920
IX Gardener,
and the surrender of Loren I Lannister.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.590
When Aegon learned that King Torrhen Stark
had crossed the Neck and was leading army

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:28.160
into the riverlands, he raced ahead of his
army on Balerion to meet the threat.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.770
When the Targaryen host was encamped at one
side of the Trident and the northern host

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:39.020
on the other side, Torrhen's brother Brandon
Snow offered to assassinate the sleeping dragons.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.820
Recalling the destruction the three dragons
had caused on the Field of Fire,

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.710
Torrhen instead submitted to Aegon.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:50.310
According to song, at the end of the war Balerion
helped to forge the Iron Throne by melting

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:53.120
the swords of Aegon's fallen enemies.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.500
Aegon treated the defeated lords with respect
and allowed each region to retain its own

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.460
laws and customs.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:03.490
Aegon often travelled with Balerion through
the realm with maesters who educated him on

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:06.690
each region's local customs and history.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:11.400
Aegon later flew Balerion into battle during
the First Dornish War, where he suffered the

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.130
greatest loss when his sister, Queen Rhaenys
Targaryen and her dragon Meraxes fell from

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:20.800
the sky after a shot from a scorpion took
the dragon in the eye.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.570
The war took a different turn after this.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:28.780
Aegon's fury and grief at the loss of his
wife was such that he headed for Dorne himself.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:34.310
Accompanied by Visenya, the last two Targaryens
rained fire upon the desert strongholds to

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:35.840
break the Dornish.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:40.420
The next two years were known as the Dragon's
Wroth, a period when every Dornish castle

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.810
felt the fury of the dragonriders.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:47.890
The only castle spared was Sunspear, the seat
of House Martell, in hopes that the Dornish

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:50.330
would turn against their liege lords.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:54.120
The strategy failed and Dorne remained unconquered.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:59.240
After Aegon's death, Balerion was claimed
by his son Prince Maegor, who had long coveted

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:05.800
his father's mount, and had not claimed another
dragon because he considered all others unworthy.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:10.980
After Jonos Arryn imprisoned his brother Lord
Ronnel and declared himself independent of

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:15.760
the Iron Throne, Maegor rode the Black Dread
to the Vale and put down his rebellion.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:21.720
When Maegor was exiled to Pentos as a punishment
for his polygamous marriage, he took Balerion

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.040
with him.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:28.170
After his brother King Aenys I died, Maegor
flew back to Westeros on Balerion to claim

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.170
the Iron Throne.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:34.840
In his reign as king, Maegor used Balerion
in the burning of the Sept of Remembrance

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:37.900
and in many other battles against the Faith
Militant.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:42.210
In the Battle Beneath the Gods Eye,
Maegor used Balerion to kill his nephew Prince

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:45.290
Aegon and his dragon Quicksilver.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:50.630
After Maegor's death, Balerion returned to
Dragonstone, where he made his lair.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:56.050
Balerion was claimed as a mount by princess
Aerea Targaryen in late 54 AC.

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.570
They disappeared and went missing for more
than a year.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:06.110
King Jaehaerys I Targaryen sent expeditions
to try and locate Balerion and the young princess,

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:10.900
and the master of coin, Rego Draz,
offered a reward for any information on their

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:14.730
whereabouts, but none came forward that were
credible.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:18.610
Balerion was the largest living dragon in
the world, but there were no sightings of

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:20.470
the dragon anywhere.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:26.580
Septon Barth believed that the lack of sightings
suggested that Balerion was no longer in Westeros.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:31.550
Balerion returned to King's Landing in 56
AC, descending into the courtyard of the Red

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:34.029
Keep with Aerea barely clinging to him.

00:08:34.029 --> 00:08:37.640
The princess was severely ill, and died soon
after.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:41.880
Barth's accounts describe wounds and half-healed
scars on Balerion.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:47.850
The dragon bore a huge jagged rent down his
left side, almost nine feet long, and fresh

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:51.760
blood still dripped from the wound, hot and
smoking.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.740
Barth speculated that, when Aerea claimed
Balerion,

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:59.759
she was unable to bend the dragon to her will,
and instead the dragon had taken her to the

00:08:59.759 --> 00:09:02.100
place he had been born, Valyria.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:06.180
What could cause such wounds to mighty Balerion
remains unknown.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:10.509
Shortly thereafter, Balerion became the first
dragon to be housed in the Dragonpit,

00:09:10.509 --> 00:09:14.019
where he was guarded by the Dragonkeepers.

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:16.259
Balerion remained at the Dragonpit.

00:09:16.259 --> 00:09:20.490
When Princess Alyssa Targaryen came to the
Dragonpit to claim a dragon of her own in

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:24.139
75 AC,
the Dragonkeepers persuaded her not to try

00:09:24.139 --> 00:09:29.341
and claim Balerion, insisting that the dragon
had become old and slow, suggesting to her

00:09:29.341 --> 00:09:32.339
that she would much more prefer a faster dragon.

00:09:32.339 --> 00:09:37.220
The last rider of Balerion was Prince Viserys
Targaryen, who entered the Dragonpit to claim

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.089
the dragon in 93 AC.

00:09:40.089 --> 00:09:45.410
Balerion was hard to rouse, and struggled
when Viserys urged him into the sky.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:49.970
They flew around King's Landing three times,
although Viserys later confided to his father

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:53.610
that he had originally intended to fly Balerion
to Dragonstone.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:10:00.100
However, fearing the dragon lacked the strength
to do so, Viserys had opted otherwise.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:05.570
Balerion died in 94 AC, less than a year after
Viserys claimed him as his mount.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:08.810
Along with eighteen other Targaryen dragon
skulls,

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:12.069
Balerion's skull hung on a wall in the Red
Keep's throne room.

00:10:12.069 --> 00:10:18.190
After Robert's Rebellion, King Robert I Baratheon
had the skulls removed from the throne room,

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.990
and stored them in a dark cellar.

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:22.699
That is the story of the mightiest Targaryen
dragon.

00:10:22.699 --> 00:10:26.990
He's seen it all and been through it all,
from the Valyrian Freehold in its prime

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:31.999
to conquering the Seven Kingdoms and living
to see generations of Targaryen's rule in

00:10:31.999 --> 00:10:32.999
Westeros.

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:35.610
Balerion was the largest dragon ever seen
in Westeros.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.230
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed
this video and if you did make sure to give

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:46.560
it a big thumbs upand I hope to see you in
the next one, peace!

